    "description": "Granted secret clearance for work at L-3 Communications\n\nWorked on two research team, the first which examine ported an encryption key management system (LCMS, a SCO UNIX based application) to a web-based platform.  The second was moving the encryption key management system to a distributed network model with multiple client applications connecting to a single Oracle database.\n\nI worked on two phases of development for encryption key generator, KP, an embedded stand-alone encryption device.  Responsibilities include design, implementation, and testing of firefly re-keying, privilege system upgrading to handle foreign key processing, platform national awareness, foreign key reconciliation, and code maintenance.",
